    "text": "Glen Lyon is a Scottish mythological site. It is a small valley in the Grampian mountains of Tayside, near Fortingall. The valley preserves an ancient survival of ritual. The tradition centers on the start of summer at Beltane on May 1. The ritual may be Celtic or even older. Many place-names recall the Cailleach, the ancient goddess or Hag. Glen Cailliche means Hag's Glen. Allt Cailliche means Hag's Stream. Tigh nam Cailliche means Hag's House.",
